## Summary

**Problem:** When stringifying a parsed path with a parameter name followed by text starting with an astral Unicode character (code point > 0xFFFF) that is an `ID_Continue` character, the `stringifyName` function failed to quote the parameter name. This broke the parse → stringify → parse round-trip.

**Root Cause:** In `stringifyName`, the check `next.value[0]` only retrieved the first UTF-16 code unit of the next text token. For astral characters (which are represented as surrogate pairs in JavaScript strings), this returned only the high surrogate, not the full Unicode code point. The `ID_CONTINUE` regex doesn't match lone surrogates, so the check incorrectly returned `false`, and the parameter name wasn't quoted.

**Fix:** Changed `next.value[0]` to `String.fromCodePoint(next.value.codePointAt(0))` in the `stringifyName` function. This properly extracts the full Unicode code point (including astral characters) and tests it against the `ID_CONTINUE` regex.

